@startuml

start

:Embedded control system employs FSM;
:Orchestrate complex real-time behavior;
fork
  :Coordinate high-priority ISRs for time-critical events;
fork again
  :Deferred processing in RTOS-managed tasks;
fork again
  :Fail-safe policy execution;
end fork

if (Sensor data > predefined thresholds?) then (yes)
  :Initialize concurrent execution paths based on operational mode;

  if (Mode?) then (Normal mode)
    fork
      repeat
      :High-priority data acquisition task samples sensors via DMA ring buffer;
      repeat while(Required sample count met) is(no)

    fork again
      :Medium-priority processing task applies;
      fork
       :Digital filtering;
      fork again
       :Calibration algorithms;
      end fork
      :Shared data access protected by mutexes;
    end fork
  else (Debug mode)
      :Spawn complementary diagnostic tasks;
      fork
        :Use exponential backoff for bus recovery;
        :Perform sensor parameter calibration;
      fork again
        :Conduct comprehensive system health checks through PMIC and BMS interfaces;
      end fork
  end if

  :Converge operational paths;
  :Generate consolidated status report;
  :With CRC-protected audit entries;
  :Write to structured ring buffer;
  :Periodically flush to non-volatile storage within strict I/O budget constraints;

else (no)
end if

fork
:Maintain system supervision;
fork
  :Watchdog monitoring;
fork again
  :Priority-based message queues;
end fork

fork again
:Execute critical FADEC/CAN bus operations in highest-priority contexts;
:Ensure deterministic response;
end fork

stop

